{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCorrectionAdmissibility","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCorrectionAdmissibility","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCarrierBarParity","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCarrierOrderWindow"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCorrectionAdmissibility.monomial_not_admissible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCorrectionAdmissibility.monomial_not_admissible","kind":"theorem","line":296,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MuPCorrectionAdmissibility.lean#L296-L325","doc":"**No small-height monomial is admissible.** For every `k, m` and every\ncoefficient with `|c| ∈ [1/5, 5]`, the function `q ↦ c·ℏ_q^k·q^m` is not an\nadmissible carrier at any pin. (Bar-evenness at `q₀`, after cancelling\n`c ≠ 0`, is the hypothesis of the capstone; positivity of the residual forces\n`c·X = |c|·X`.) Dropping `hc0` admits `c = t/w³ ≈ 0.162` at `(k, m) = (6, 3)`\nas a member — the exclusion is the small-height bound, as designed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCorrectionAdmissibility.GapA4CorrectionAdmissible.carries_residual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCorrectionAdmissibility.GapA4CorrectionAdmissible.carries_residual","kind":"theorem","line":294,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MuPCorrectionAdmissibility.lean#L294-L294","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCorrectionAdmissibility.GapA4CorrectionAdmissible.bar_even_at_pin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCorrectionAdmissibility.GapA4CorrectionAdmissible.bar_even_at_pin","kind":"theorem","line":293,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MuPCorrectionAdmissibility.lean#L293-L293","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCorrectionAdmissibility.GapA4CorrectionAdmissible.pin_window","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCorrectionAdmissibility.GapA4CorrectionAdmissible.pin_window","kind":"theorem","line":292,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MuPCorrectionAdmissibility.lean#L292-L292","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCorrectionAdmissibility.GapA4CorrectionAdmissible.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCorrectionAdmissibility.GapA4CorrectionAdmissible.mk","kind":"ctor","line":291,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MuPCorrectionAdmissibility.lean#L291-L291","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCorrectionAdmissibility.GapA4CorrectionAdmissible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCorrectionAdmissibility.GapA4CorrectionAdmissible","kind":"structure","line":271,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MuPCorrectionAdmissibility.lean#L271-L294","doc":"**Admissible GAP-A-4 correction factor.** A function `F : ℝ → ℝ` of the\nsubstrate modulus is an admissible carrier of the μ–p residual at the pin `q₀`\nwhen\n\n* `pin_window` — the pin lies in the window `[1.1099, 1.11]` (which contains\n  the proton pin `1.10997858275138`);\n* `bar_even_at_pin` — `F` is fixed by the bar involution **at the pin**,\n  `F q₀⁻¹ = F q₀`. The corpus's precondition is bar-evenness as a function of\n  `q`; that implies this field, so every function bar-even everywhere is in\n  the class, and the exclusion below therefore covers the larger class. (This\n  is also exactly the instance the proof uses.)\n* `carries_residual` — evaluated at the pin, `F` lands in the residual window\n  `[1.8e-7, 2.4e-7]` around the measured `t ≈ 2.1e-7`.\n\nEvery field is content-bearing. **The structure is a filter, not a\ncertificate.** It is trivially inhabited — the constant function\n`fun _ => 2/10⁷` at `q₀ = 1.1099` satisfies all three fields — so membership\nencodes no derivation whatever, and `F ∈ GapA4CorrectionAdmissible` must never\nbe cited as evidence that a correction exists. Its only content is which\nfunctions are *excluded* from it: `monomial_not_admissible` below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCorrectionAdmissibility.no_bar_even_small_height_monomial_hbarQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCorrectionAdmissibility.no_bar_even_small_height_monomial_hbarQ","kind":"theorem","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MuPCorrectionAdmissibility.lean#L254-L267","doc":"The capstone against the **production** substrate `hbarQ` (from\n`MmuR9V9Closure`), via the bridge `hbarGen_eq_hbarQ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCorrectionAdmissibility.no_bar_even_small_height_monomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCorrectionAdmissibility.no_bar_even_small_height_monomial","kind":"theorem","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MuPCorrectionAdmissibility.lean#L231-L252","doc":"**No bar-even small-height monomial carries the μ–p residual.** If\n`ℏ_q^k · q^m` is bar-even (`hbar`), `q` lies in the pin window, `|c| ∈ [1/5, 5]`\nand `t` in the residual window, then `|c|·ℏ_q^k·q^m ≠ t`.\n\nBar-evenness forces `k = 2m` (`bar_even_monomial_iff`), the positive half of\nthe selection rule rewrites the monomial as `w^m`\n(`hbarGen_pow_two_mul_eq_wGen_pow`), and `no_small_height_w_monomial` excludes\nevery `m`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCorrectionAdmissibility.no_small_height_w_monomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCorrectionAdmissibility.no_small_height_w_monomial","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MuPCorrectionAdmissibility.lean#L191-L227","doc":"**The `w`-tower carries no small-height residual** (Lean form of the\nprobe's measured `t/w³ = 0.1621 < 1/5`, `t/w⁴ = 14.88 > 5` at the CODATA-2018\nratio; `0.1632` and `14.98` at CODATA-2022 — see the module docstring). For every\norder `j`, a monomial `|c|·w^j` with `|c| ∈ [1/5, 5]` and `q` in the pin\nwindow misses the residual window `t ∈ [1.8e-7, 2.4e-7]`.\n\nOrders `j ≤ 3` give at least `(1/5)·(108/10000)³ ≈ 2.52e-7`, above the top of\nthe window; orders `j ≥ 4` give at most `5·(11/1000)⁴ ≈ 7.32e-8`, below the\nbottom. Both are contradictions; the proof mirrors `order_window`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCorrectionAdmissibility.wGen_upper_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCorrectionAdmissibility.wGen_upper_bound","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MuPCorrectionAdmissibility.lean#L177-L187","doc":"`w ≤ 0.011` on the window: `q ≤ 1.11` and `q⁻¹ ≤ 10000/11099` give\n`w ≤ 1.11 + 10000/11099 − 2 = 0.011 − 199/11099000`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCorrectionAdmissibility.wGen_lower_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCorrectionAdmissibility.wGen_lower_bound","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MuPCorrectionAdmissibility.lean#L165-L175","doc":"`w ≥ 0.0108` on the window: `q ≥ 1.1099` and `q⁻¹ ≥ 100/111` give\n`w ≥ 1.1099 + 100/111 − 2 = 0.0108 + 1/1110000`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCorrectionAdmissibility.bar_even_monomial_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCorrectionAdmissibility.bar_even_monomial_iff","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MuPCorrectionAdmissibility.lean#L124-L157","doc":"**Selection rule, both halves.** Over `ℝ` with `1 < q`, the monomial\n`ℏ_q^k · q^m` is bar-even — `ℏ_{q⁻¹}^k · (q⁻¹)^m = ℏ_q^k · q^m` — **iff**\n`k = 2m`.\n\nForward direction: `hbarGen_bar` turns the left side into\n`(−q)^k · ℏ_q^k · (q⁻¹)^m`; cancelling `ℏ_q^k ≠ 0` and clearing `(q⁻¹)^m`\nleaves `(−q)^k = q^{2m}`; taking absolute values gives `q^k = q^{2m}`, and\n`n ↦ q^n` is injective for `q > 1`. Converse: `hbarGen_monomial_bar_even`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCorrectionAdmissibility.hbarGen_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MuPCorrectionAdmissibility.hbarGen_pos","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MuPCorrectionAdmissibility.lean#L118-L122","doc":"On `1 < q` the substrate is positive: `ℏ_q = 1 − q⁻¹ > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}